# §4: generated exports are never committed
exports/

# The three hand-authored fixtures are contractual content and stay on the machine that
# made them (F04). `tests/fixtures/manifest.json` is committed in their place: it carries
# their SHA-256 only, so a sign-off can name the exact bytes it was made against without
# the bytes ever entering the repository.
#
# Listed by name rather than as `*.docx`: the built stand-ins (`built_*.docx`,
# `degraded.docx`) are generated from raw OOXML, carry no customer content, and are
# committed on purpose so the suite covers those cases while the Word files are
# outstanding. A wildcard here would quietly fight them.
#
# Consequence, stated once so it is a decision and not a surprise: CI never sees the
# hand-authored files, so it runs against the stand-ins. `tests/fixtures/README.md`
# remains the contract for what each file must contain.
tests/fixtures/constructs.docx
tests/fixtures/revisions.docx
tests/fixtures/containers.docx
